  "application_type_full": "Householder planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed roof extension, by reason of its scale, form and siting, would introduce an incongruous and visually intrusive form of development that would fail to relate appropriately to the traditional pitched roof form of the host building and run of terraced properties. The development would result in significant harm to the architectural integrity and established character of the property and the western terraced street scene to which it forms part. The proposal represents poor design that would not be visually well integrated within its context. The development is therefore contrary to Policies LP1 and LP5 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the guidance set out in the Housing SPD (2016).\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to work with the applicant in a positive and proactive manner and the Council has, as far as practicable, sought solutions to problems arising in relation to dealing with the planning application. We have made available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan, Supplementary Planning documents and where appropriate the Site Specific Allocations Document as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
